<item>
            <title>[LU-20927] sanity test_271f: Timeout occurred after 316 minutes, last suite running was sanity</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20927</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Session 6777ca3c-1678-454e-8559-3dae133f80df (change 68650 ps4, job&lt;br/&gt;
lustre-reviews-lustre-b2_16-el9.4-x86_64_lustre-reviews-el9.7-x86_64-custom,&lt;br/&gt;
RHEL 9.7 client/ldiskfs, retest of a421cc74-00f7-4f9b-b767-77dca8e02a9a):&lt;br/&gt;
the whole sanity suite hit Autotest&apos;s wall-clock limit while test_271f&lt;br/&gt;
(DoM: read on open) was running; the suite log shows the test start a&lt;br/&gt;
dd of a 200K file at 09:18:12 and then nothing further for the&lt;br/&gt;
remaining 316 minutes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This exact signature (Timeout occurred after N minutes, last suite&lt;br/&gt;
running was sanity) has not failed before or since: rainshadow test&lt;br/&gt;
sanity test_271f shows error_history count 1, this session only, and&lt;br/&gt;
no suggested ticket fits a TIMEOUT by its error (&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19027&quot; title=&quot;sanity test_271d test_271f: -1 resend occured&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-19027&quot;&gt;LU-19027&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20662&quot; title=&quot;sanity test_271f: &quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20662&quot;&gt;LU-20662&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
and &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-15884&quot; title=&quot;sanity test_271f: expect 1 READ RPC, 2 occured&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-15884&quot;&gt;LU-15884&lt;/a&gt; are all about &quot;-1 resend occured&quot; assertion failures in&lt;br/&gt;
test_271f, a different failure mode from a suite-level hang).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The console logs for this session show repeated, unrelated MDT/MGS&lt;br/&gt;
connection losses and evictions scattered through the whole run&lt;br/&gt;
(e.g. vm16 05:47:10, vm18 05:39:57/05:40:13, vm17 09:15:22), well&lt;br/&gt;
before and unrelated to test_271f&apos;s start, consistent with transient&lt;br/&gt;
test-fleet network instability rather than a test or Lustre defect.&lt;br/&gt;
No lock waits, stuck Lustre service threads or crash signatures were&lt;br/&gt;
found in the stack-trace dumps taken at the timeout (--hang found no&lt;br/&gt;
matches; the only D-state task is &quot;lctl&quot; itself gathering the dump).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Change 68650 touches only lustre/osc/osc_request.c and&lt;br/&gt;
lustre/include/lustre_net.h (bulk MD alignment for old servers); it&lt;br/&gt;
has no connection to DoM read-on-open, FIEMAP, or the MDT/MGS&lt;br/&gt;
reconnect path, so this is not the patch&apos;s.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-68650-ps4-ea7444aefb42 on &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/68650&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/68650&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
